WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:05.823
- First up, coming in, Roshan saying,

00:00:05.823 --> 00:00:08.792
"I'm an introvert, being introverted,

00:00:08.792 --> 00:00:11.717
how can I develop my
communication skills?"

00:00:11.717 --> 00:00:14.493
What advice would have
there for introvert Roshan?

00:00:14.493 --> 00:00:17.691
- Hey Roshan, now I've got
some great news for you.

00:00:17.691 --> 00:00:19.818
I'll use a couple of other
quotes actually from people

00:00:19.818 --> 00:00:23.213
I think both Evan and I respect,

00:00:23.213 --> 00:00:24.145
who are amazing,

00:00:24.145 --> 00:00:27.722
but they're introverts and
I think we often forget,

00:00:27.722 --> 00:00:30.242
we kind of have, I think actually,

00:00:30.242 --> 00:00:33.321
part of social media and
the celebrity culture,

00:00:33.321 --> 00:00:36.050
you kind of expect everybody
to be an extrovert out there.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:40.034
But they're not, when
people are very authentic

00:00:40.034 --> 00:00:41.851
a lot of people are introverts.

00:00:41.851 --> 00:00:44.095
You know, Evan shared with you before

00:00:44.095 --> 00:00:47.121
on previous broadcasts about you know

00:00:47.121 --> 00:00:50.231
how he's overcome and maybe
he'll talk a bit about that

00:00:50.231 --> 00:00:52.451
today but one guy we both met and we think

00:00:52.451 --> 00:00:54.848
pretty amazing entrepreneur,
Richard Branson,

00:00:54.848 --> 00:00:59.585
his quote is "I had to train
myself into become more

00:00:59.585 --> 00:01:01.237
of an extrovert."

00:01:01.237 --> 00:01:04.244
I mean we've both met the
guy, he's just very humble,

00:01:04.244 --> 00:01:08.005
super nice guy, cares
passionately about customers,

00:01:08.005 --> 00:01:11.423
always looking for the way
to disrupt an industry.

00:01:11.423 --> 00:01:14.198
And then another one from a
completely different field,

00:01:14.198 --> 00:01:17.040
someone who wrote all the
legendary Harry Potter books,

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:21.538
JK Rowling, she said, "I've
been writing almost continuously

00:01:21.538 --> 00:01:25.145
since the age of six, but
I've never been so excited

00:01:25.145 --> 00:01:29.958
about this idea like I have
then. But my intense, immense

00:01:29.958 --> 00:01:33.849
frustration is I didn't
have a pen that worked,

00:01:33.849 --> 00:01:38.016
and I was too shy to ask
anybody if I could borrow one."

00:01:38.016 --> 00:01:40.141
You know, and that's
one of the most numery

00:01:40.141 --> 00:01:41.760
authors of our times.

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:44.691
And then someone in our
industry, Bill Gates,

00:01:44.691 --> 00:01:47.725
whose done amazing philanthropic
work around the world

00:01:47.725 --> 00:01:49.286
and leading massive campaigns

00:01:49.286 --> 00:01:51.204
to do things like stop malaria,

00:01:51.204 --> 00:01:53.140
and obviously built Microsoft.

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:54.830
And he kind of acknowledges,

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:56.827
you know I think introverts
can do pretty well.

00:01:56.827 --> 00:01:59.596
If you're clever you can
learn to get to the benefits

00:01:59.596 --> 00:02:01.501
of being a really good introvert,

00:02:01.501 --> 00:02:03.251
about thinking about really top problems.

00:02:03.251 --> 00:02:05.819
About kind of reading
everything you can just to

00:02:05.819 --> 00:02:07.235
push yourself very hard,

00:02:07.235 --> 00:02:11.587
to think of the edge and
beyond the edge of your area.

00:02:11.587 --> 00:02:14.345
But you'd better team
up with some extroverts

00:02:14.345 --> 00:02:17.456
that kind of do and tap
into both sets of skills,

00:02:17.456 --> 00:02:18.959
so that you can build a company

00:02:18.959 --> 00:02:21.486
and thrive both the deep thinking

00:02:21.486 --> 00:02:24.975
but building a team also
to go out to the world

00:02:24.975 --> 00:02:27.317
and sell those ideas.

00:02:27.317 --> 00:02:29.400
So what does that mean?

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:31.314
It means there's a lot of
people around the world

00:02:31.314 --> 00:02:32.893
you should feel very comfortable,

00:02:32.893 --> 00:02:35.113
you know that a lot of
great business people,

00:02:35.113 --> 00:02:38.477
a lot of great entrepreneurs
are absolutely introvert.

00:02:38.477 --> 00:02:42.222
And I think my most sort of humble advice

00:02:42.222 --> 00:02:44.170
would be with all these things

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:46.225
is we talked about with people
like Martin Luther King,

00:02:46.225 --> 00:02:48.594
take that first step on
that giant staircase,

00:02:48.594 --> 00:02:51.752
and the easier, you know the
more you pitch your idea,

00:02:51.752 --> 00:02:53.895
the more you pitch it
to friends and family

00:02:53.895 --> 00:02:55.486
in the society, in the environment,

00:02:55.486 --> 00:02:56.803
more confidence you get.

00:02:56.803 --> 00:03:01.175
And you can definitely overcome
your level of introversion

00:03:01.175 --> 00:03:03.274
and be very successful.

00:03:03.274 --> 00:03:04.228
What are your thoughts Evan?

00:03:04.228 --> 00:03:06.005
Cuz you know you've been very

00:03:06.005 --> 00:03:07.612
you've shown a lot of humility

00:03:07.612 --> 00:03:09.971
and humanity in this topic

00:03:09.971 --> 00:03:12.223
and it's a very personal topic to you.

00:03:12.223 --> 00:03:14.368
- Yeah, I mean we talked about this

00:03:14.368 --> 00:03:18.613
in the last one or time before
how we were both introverted.

00:03:18.613 --> 00:03:21.185
And it may not always feel like it,

00:03:21.185 --> 00:03:24.618
watching us on these sessions
but we're both introverted.

00:03:24.618 --> 00:03:28.454
And first of all I think
it's just understanding that

00:03:28.454 --> 00:03:31.037
being an introvert can
actually be a strength for you

00:03:31.037 --> 00:03:32.465
in the ability to communicate.

00:03:32.465 --> 00:03:35.600
Because yes you have to learn to talk,

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:37.361
but you have to learn to talk in a way

00:03:37.361 --> 00:03:38.695
that other people can understand.

00:03:38.695 --> 00:03:40.384
I think introverts
actually do a better job

00:03:40.384 --> 00:03:44.722
of listening so that you can
understand the other person.

00:03:44.722 --> 00:03:47.014
And so where extroverts
maybe need to do a better job

00:03:47.014 --> 00:03:47.847
of listening,

00:03:47.847 --> 00:03:49.062
introverts have that already,

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:51.648
and so just tapping into
that listening ability,

00:03:51.648 --> 00:03:55.208
to know what they want, to
hear what they're excited about

00:03:55.208 --> 00:03:57.309
and then give them a
message that will hit home.

00:03:57.309 --> 00:04:00.429
And so first off for me would just be

00:04:00.429 --> 00:04:04.272
disassociating the idea that
because I am an introvert

00:04:04.272 --> 00:04:08.572
I can't be a success at
being a communicator.

00:04:08.572 --> 00:04:11.064
Well you can, you just
do it in a different way.

00:04:11.064 --> 00:04:12.829
You do it by listening really intently

00:04:12.829 --> 00:04:14.086
and then sharing your message.

00:04:14.086 --> 00:04:17.262
You don't have to be yelling
at the front of a stage

00:04:17.262 --> 00:04:19.078
to communicate, there's
a lot of different ways

00:04:19.078 --> 00:04:20.543
to get your message out there.

00:04:20.543 --> 00:04:22.697
I don't think you should,

00:04:22.697 --> 00:04:24.589
I don't think you need
to become that person

00:04:24.589 --> 00:04:26.137
who's yelling on stage.

00:04:26.137 --> 00:04:28.737
Go all in on your strengths,

00:04:28.737 --> 00:04:30.847
and use that ability to listen really well

00:04:30.847 --> 00:04:33.056
to give a message that
really resonates with the

00:04:33.056 --> 00:04:36.556
person that you're trying to connect with.

